# Copy to receiver.env and set the explicit Codex session that must receive
# WORK_ANALYSIS_REPORT messages. Never use `resume --last` here.
SESSION_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Optional override. On Windows the receiver also discovers the newest Codex
# binary bundled with the VS Code/VS Code Insiders extension when Task
# Scheduler's PATH cannot find codex.exe.
# Git Bash example:
# CODEX_BIN=/c/Users/Owner/.vscode/extensions/openai.chatgpt-<version>-win32-x64/bin/windows-x86_64/codex.exe

# Automatic drop folder: .codex-monitor/incoming/
# Write a schema-v1 JSON report completely under a temporary filename, then
# atomically rename it to *.ready.json. Markdown inputs are intentionally rejected.
# The scheduled worker validates, accepts, processes, and audits it without loss.
